{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517080-ahrimane-bloodline","id":1517080,"title":"Ahrimane Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-03T10:03:28-07:00","id":1517080,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Ahrimane Bloodline","content":"\u200bThis is a (very) rough first draft of the Ahrimane bloodline ported over from World of Darkness. I have dropped the &quot;all female&quot; portion for the time being, I'm not sure if I'll bring it back or not. I was also wanting to create a bloodline tied to the devourering of Ravening Wolf and I figured that sense the Ahrimane clan's primary discipline was centered around spirits they would be a good fit for that.<br /> <br /> I had originally planned for them to be an offshoot of the Gangrel, but as I was looking their original disciplines were Animalism, Spiritus, and Presence, and then their disciplines in DAV20 were Animalism, Spiritus, and Potence and I really didn't wish to give a Gangrel bloodline I was creating either Presence or Potence. So I looked to the Daeva who already had both of those disciplines and only really lacked animalism as a clan discipline for what I wanted.<br /> <br /> I had originally thought to use the idea of the Ghost Blooded Tyrants ruling Sumer to die in the Daeva, but Sumer and Mongolia are a fair distance apart so I wasn't sure how that would work. Still, the Daeva dating back to the Ancient Babylonian empire and being located in Asia did work for my purposes so that's something at least.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure I'm in love with their weakness. I know I want the Daeva clan weakness to apply to spirits and not just mortals, but I'm considering something more spirit based than what I have now (which is just a variation of their WoD weakness).<br /> <br /> If anyone has any suggestions I'll be happy to listen to them, I have only a rudimentary knowledge of Requiem. And again, this is a very rough first draft, the writing is mostly train of thought. <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Ahrimanes: The Ones Who Resist the Spirits</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Don't blame me, blame my friends on the other side.&quot;</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">On the steppes of Asia in times of old a ravenous beast roamed, seeking who it might devour. It was too destructive for us to ignore and too strong for us to oppose outright and so we sought out a way to defeat it. Eventually, we discovered the thing's bane, while it was driven to devour everything it could not resist being devoured itself. So we laid a trap, separated it from its followers, and fell upon it en masse. We drained it, but it, it changed us, opened our eyes to the world beyond, but it also opened the eyes of those in the world beyond to us as well. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">For millennia we were the Kindred's first line of defense against the spirit world. We warned the Julii of the dangers the Strix possessed and watched our warning be ignored. Even so many blamed us for all that happened, we were hated and hunted. Fleeing that, many of our eldest withdrew from the Requiem and sought the sleep of ages and others hid themselves until even the memory of our bloodline passed. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">But our eldest have awakened and have brought a warning. Our ancient foe, whom we slew so long ago, walks the world once more. The kindred have need of us again, even if they don't yet know it. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Why you want to be us</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">We are the masters of this world, our wills command the beasts, our desires ignite the passions of mortals, our strength is second to none. But more than that, we have powers beyond this world. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Why you should fear us</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">We have powers you can never understand, we entreat with entities from beyond this world. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Why we should fear ourselves</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Dealing with the spirit world is not without risks, or consequences. Overconfident Ahrimanes are not long for this world and even the wisest can make a mistake over the millennia. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Parent Clan:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Daeva</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Nicknames: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Animists, Spirit Hunters (mockingly)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Bloodline Bane (The Upright Curse): </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The blood of the Ahrimane is weakened, the creation of a ghoul requires an additional willpower point be spent (in addition to the viate and the normal willpower cost), and the embrace requires a dot of willpower be spent in addition to other costs. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Additionally the Daeva clan bane applies to spirits the vampire feeds from, as well as mortals.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><b>Disciplines:</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Animalism, Blood Tenebrous*, </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>Majesty</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">, Vigor</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">*Blood Tenebrous was introduced in the Book of Spirits for first edition and is updated to 2</span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><sup><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">nd</span></sup></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> edition in Ephemeral Influence. If the Storyteller chooses to make version of Blood Tenebrous that effect ghosts and the Underworld or goetia and the Astral, only the spirit version of Blood Tenebrous is a clan discipline for the Ahrimanes</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>In the Covenants:</b><br /> <br /> The Lancea Et Sanctum has virtually no Ahrimane members. Their views are just not compatible with the spirit world that the Ahrimane deal with.<br /> <br /> The Carthian Movement, likewise, has few Ahrimane, they are too involved with the spirits to worry overly much about the mortal political movements.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul has a fair number of Ahrimane among their numbers, many of whom believe that to ascend vampirism would allow them to fully become spirits.<br /> <br /> The Invictus claims a large number of Ahrimane, their abilities to deal with the world beyond give them a leg up on much of their competition and feeds their belief that they should rule.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone also claims a large number of Ahrimane, their beliefs align best with the spirit world the Ahrimane deal with and the Ahrimane appreciate the blood magic of the Circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T11:12:00-07:00","id":1517084,"title":"","content":"Don't have Ephemeral Influence so I don't know how this interacts with that version of Blood Tenebrous. If Blood Tenebrous is able to shut these influences down, add a rider that the Ahrimane's Blood Tenebrous can't use the Discipline to shut down the Haunted Curse.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Haunted Curse):</b> Predatory and unclean spirits stir when they smell the dead blood of their precursors curdled in the vampire's veins. The presence of the Ahrimane grants such spirits the Resonant and Open Influence Conditions. In addition, the Ahrimane extends the Wanton Curse of the Daeva to spirits as well as mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T11:56:09-07:00","id":1517085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517080-ahrimane-bloodline?p=1517084#post1517084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't have Ephemeral Influence so I don't know how this interacts with that version of Blood Tenebrous. If Blood Tenebrous is able to shut these influences down, add a rider that the Ahrimane's Blood Tenebrous can't use the Discipline to shut down the Haunted Curse.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Bane (The Haunted Curse):</b> Predatory and unclean spirits stir when they smell the dead blood of their precursors curdled in the vampire's veins. The presence of the Ahrimane grants such spirits the Resonant and Open Influence Conditions. In addition, the Ahrimane extends the Wanton Curse of the Daeva to spirits as well as mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had considered going that way, but blood tenebrous grants those conditions when used, which is part of it being dangerous to use and I didn't want to overlap too much. I love your wording on the last sentence though, I will definitely use that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T12:07:27-07:00","id":1517087,"title":"","content":"Does just knowing Blood Tenebrous impose them permanently? Because there's a big difference between &quot;spirits can use their Manifestations and Numina around me freely when I want them to be able to&quot; and &quot;spirits can use their Manifestations and Numina around me freely <i>all the time</i> and I don't get a say in it.&quot;<br /> <br /> That &quot;predatory and unclean spirits&quot; language also isn't just flavor text. This bane only applies to spirits of murder, disease, predatory animals, etc. <i>Those </i>get to haunt you and those around you. While any spirit is in some sense predatory among its own kind, if you want to facilitate contact with spirits of traffic lights, knowledge, healing, shadows, fire, or any number of other resonances, you use Blood Tenebrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T12:12:59-07:00","id":1517088,"title":"","content":"No, it isn't a permanent thing, only while the discipline is in use so I see your point. I like that. I think I will go that route. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T06:25:05-07:00","id":1521326,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><b>Ahrimanes: The ones who walk by shadow</b><br /> <br /> On the steppes of Asia in times of old a ravenous beast roamed, seeking who it might devour. It was too destructive for us to ignore and too strong for us to oppose outright and so we sought out a way to defeat it. Eventually, we discovered the thing's bane, while it was driven to devour everything it could not resist being devoured itself. So we laid a trap, separated it from its followers, and fell upon it en masse. We drained it, but it, it changed us, opened our eyes to the world beyond, but it also opened the eyes of those in the world beyond to us as well.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">In the ancient city of Sumer, we loved the wolves and shared our thrones for them to rule in the day as we ruled in the night. The wolves, in return, shared with us a new world of spirit and shadow. That city is gone now, and none among the wolves remember it or the love they had beneath our fangs, but we remember them and the world they showed us.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Long ago a spirit and a vampire courted a beautiful young maiden. The spirit claimed her first, but the vampire embraced her best. Still through her long night she longed for her first love, until she discovered a way they could be together again. She is still out there, somewhere, united forever with her two loves, and we, her children, carry on. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><b>Why you want to be us</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">We are the masters of this world, our wills command the beasts, our desires ignite the passions of mortals, our strength is second to none. But more than that, we have powers beyond this world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><b>Why you should fear us</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">We have powers you can never understand, we entreat with entities from the shadow of this world.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><b>Why we should fear ourselves</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Dealing with the spirit world is not without risks, or consequences. Overconfident Ahrimanes are not long for this world and even the wisest can make a mistake over the millennia.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><b>Parent Clan: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Daeva</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><b>Nicknames: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Animists, Spirit Hunters (mockingly)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><b>Bloodline Bane (The Haunted Curse): </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Predatory and unclean spirits stir when they smell the dead blood of their precursors curdled in the vampire's veins. The presence of the Ahrimane grants such spirits the Resonant and Open Influence Conditions. In addition, the Ahrimane extends the Wanton Curse of the Daeva to spirits as well as mortals.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><b>Disciplines: </b></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Animalism, Blood Tenebrous*, </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><i>Majesty</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">, Vigor<br /> *Blood Tenebrous was introduced in the Book of Spirits for first edition and is updated to 2</span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><sup><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:8px\">nd</span></span></sup></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">edition in Ephemeral Influence. If the Storyteller chooses to make versions of Blood Tenebrous that effect ghosts and the Underworld or goetia and the Astral, only the spirit version of Blood Tenebrous is a clan discipline for the Ahrimanes</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><b>In the Covenants:</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">The Lancea Et Sanctum has virtually no Ahrimane members. Their views are just not compatible with the spirit world that the Ahrimane deal with. Likewise the Sanctum would be happy to slay the Ahrimanes as heretics.<br /> The Carthian Movement has few Ahrimane, they are too involved with the spirits to worry overly much about the mortal political movements.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">The Invictus claim scarcely more Ahrimane than the movement, but those it does claim tend to be brutal and effective, using spirits to spy on rivals and to disrupt anything that might threaten them or the conspiracy of silence.<br /> The Ordo Dracul has a fair number of Ahrimane among their numbers, many of whom believe that to ascend vampirism would allow them to fully become spirits.<br /> The Circle of the Crone also claims a large number of Ahrimane, their beliefs align best with the spirit world the Ahrimane deal with and the Ahrimane appreciate the blood magic of the Circle.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Unnamed Merit (Ahrimane only):</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">* Humans (or animals) you feed on gain the resonant condition. At level 4 of this merit this increases to them gaining the open condition. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">** You can speak and understand the language of spirits gaining the First Tongue as an additional language.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">*** By this stage the blood of the Ahrimane is especially tuned to spirits, they gain 9 again on all rolls for summoning, binding, warding, abjuring or exorcising spirits as well as dice rolls for Blood Tenebrous. (Use Humanity as integrity and use mask for vice and dirge for virtue when need be.) Or perhaps this would be better allowing for blood to be spent to increase dice to these rolls ala physical intensity? </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">**** When binding, exorcising, or feeding (with blood tenubous) from a spirit you may learn a portion of it's essence, gaining a single influence that it possesses at level 2. You may spend a will power point to give up your influence so that you may gain a different influence. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">***** When binding, exorcising, or feeding (with blood tenubous) from a spirit you may spend 4 experience to learn a Numina that it knows that does not rely on Manifestations. You may fuel the Numina either with viate as though it were essence, or with essence if you have an essence pool. You may have a maximum number of Numina equal to your resolve and may spend experience to replace ones you no longer desire. Roll Resolve + Occult + Blood Potency to activate numinia. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Unnamed Devotion:</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Blood Tenebrous **, Majesty ** This devotion costs 2 xp.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Cost: 1 Willpower</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">While feeding from a spirit or allowing one to feed from you, you may bargain with the spirit to trade your discipline dots for its numinia or influence dots on a 1:1 basis. Presence (or Manipulation) + Occult \u2013 spirit's resistance. Take an additional penalty to the roll equal to the essence you have drained from the spirit, or a bonus equal to the amount of viate you have given the spirit. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Success: Spirit is willing to do the trade. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Duration: 1 Night. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><b>Friends on the Other Side</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">Blood Tenebrous ***, And Either Majesty **, Animalism **, or Vigor **</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">This power allows you to turn spirits who drink your viate into ghouls as well as to create blood bonds on spirits following the normal rules for those effects. Majesty allows this power to effect Conceptual spirits, Animalism allows this power to effect Nature spirits, and Vigor allows this power to effect Artificial spirits. If there is a version of this power that effects Elemental spirits or Magath, it has not been discovered.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">This power has one side effect, if a spirit would be killed within 3 nights of having fed on viate it instead transforms into a magath with undeath as it's second type, and reforms in a safe place with a single point of essence in hibernation rather than being slain. It may trade any of its current influence or any of its numinia in for Influence: Undead. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">This power costs 2 xp the first time it is purchased, but it may be purchased multiple times if the requiements for the different versions are met. It costs only 1 xp on subsequent purchases.</span></span>\u200b</b><br /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T09:02:59-07:00","id":1521331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517080-ahrimane-bloodline?p=1521326#post1521326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Inherit\">* Humans (or animals) you feed on gain the resonant condition. At level 4 of this merit this increases to them gaining the open condition. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>You're gonna want to define what kind of resonance this is. A person, place or thing typically isn't just Resonant or not Resonant. Rather, what one spirit finds Resonant another spirit doesn't. The resonance has a character. Fire spirits might experience the presence of fire, heat, or smoke as Resonant. Cat spirits are going to treat the presence of cats as Resonant. A wood spirit might treat a board of plywood and a living tree as both Resonant, while a carpentry spirit might experience resonance around the plywood but not the living tree. It's better to think of Resonant as what happens when a spirit finds the qualities it's seeking out, not an objective quality of the person or place that exists independently of the spirit.<br /> <br /> Now, you <i>can</i> design magical effects that impose Resonant regardless of the relevance of a spirit to the thing being made Resonant. That's not a thing you can't do. But consider that if you're not either a) specifying which spirit or type of spirit is being made Resonant with the target (like &quot;any spirit you have blood bound treats this character as Resonant for your Blood Potency in nights&quot;) or b) specifying a type of resonance so that you can determine which spirits do and do not resonate with it (like &quot;the character becomes Resonant for spirits of death, disease, and misfortune until the next sunset&quot;), just generic Resonant or Open would make a character a magnet for <i>all</i> spirits. Even the Shadow Realm across the Gauntlet is going to react to the target's presence, because you've just made a source of food that everything, regardless of its place on the food chain or typical diet, can eat.<br /> <br /> It also kind of makes a lot of applications of Blood Tenebrous irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 08-24-2023, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T10:02:37-07:00","id":1521333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517080-ahrimane-bloodline?p=1521331#post1521331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're gonna want to define what kind of resonance this is. A person, place or thing typically isn't just Resonant or not Resonant.</div> </div> </div> </div>The intention was that it would be resonant for all spirits, I will fix my wording there. I'd actually had level 1 as &quot;gain the spirit specialty in Occult&quot; and changed it just this morning because &quot;gain a specialty&quot; is done so much in these rip offs of cult initiation type merits. <br /> <br /> I would point out that being fed upon likely makes the character resonant for a significant number of spirits without this merit. Spirits of pleasure / joy would find a mortal experiencing the kiss resonant. Spirits resonant with fear or violence would find the assault form of feeding more their type. Spirits with weakness or loss as part of their purview may also find victims of feeding to be a good target. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now, you <i>can</i> design magical effects that impose Resonant regardless of the relevance of a spirit to the thing being made Resonant. That's not a thing you can't do. But consider that if you're not either a) specifying which spirit or type of spirit is being made Resonant with the target (like &quot;any spirit you have blood bound treats this character as Resonant for your Blood Potency in nights&quot;) or b) specifying a type of resonance so that you can determine which spirits do and do not resonate with it (like &quot;the character becomes Resonant for spirits of death, disease, and misfortune until the next sunset&quot;), just generic Resonant or Open would make a character a magnet for <i>all</i> spirits. Even the Shadow Realm across the Gauntlet is going to react to the target's presence, because you've just made a source of food that everything, regardless of its place on the food chain or typical diet, can eat. </div> </div> </div>The intention is that the mortal is a magnet for all spirits, though magnet is probably a bit strong of a phrase for just the resonant condition. (I think magnet is pretty fair for the open condition.) It can give a vampire a bargaining chip &quot;I'll make a person open for you if you'll do something for me&quot; but it can also be problematic &quot;oh shit, the person I was eating just got possessed.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It also kind of makes a lot of applications of Blood Tenebrous irrelevant. </div> </div> </div>I don't get how you think that. Can you explain your thought process here? <br /> <br /> To me it's the opposite, it makes Blood Tenebrous more relevant. If any human or animal you feed from could get possessed at any moment, being able to look around twilight and see what's around seems more important than it was before, ditto being able to interact with beings within twilight. Being able to transform your viate into a universal bane seems extra useful if you're encountering more people being possessed, etc. <br /> <br /> Ultimately this was largely intended to be a way to make a character's life more interesting and give an additional reason for the Ahrimane to be interacting with spirits, if it's not doing that, or it's doing too much it may have to be changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T10:32:12-07:00","id":1521338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517080-ahrimane-bloodline?p=1521333#post1521333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get how you think that. Can you explain your thought process here?</div> </div> </div> </div>It sounds like you're approaching Blood Tenebrous primarily from the standpoint of obstructing and defeating spirits, but it's also a Discipline of mediumship. (Well, I don't know exactly how Ephemeral Influence converts it.) You use it to fight enemy spirits, yes, but also to make spirits your <i>allies</i> and bring them into Twilight where they can use their power in ways that serve you both. And one of the main things preventing a spirit from being able to follow an ally from the Shadow Realm into Twilight and aid them is a lack of Influence Conditions to sustain them where they go. If you've got a source of no-cost, universal Influence Conditions tagged onto a basic action you're already taking all the time, the role of using your Discipline as an art of mediumship is obviated.<br /> <br /> I think it makes for a lot more interesting play if your vampire is courting spirit allies and ushering them through Twilight to use their power on her behalf rather than having extra bolt-on powers that just let her internalize the spirits' powers directly.<br /> <br /> It's also a bit much to stack on top of the bloodline bane I suggested, which already has <i>you</i> acting as a magnet for a bunch of spirits with vampire-adjacent resonance. Too much resonance all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T11:46:12-07:00","id":1521343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1517080-ahrimane-bloodline?p=1521338#post1521338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It sounds like you're approaching Blood Tenebrous primarily from the standpoint of obstructing and defeating spirits, but it's also a Discipline of mediumship. (Well, I don't know exactly how Ephemeral Influence converts it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Levels 1 and 5 are mostly the same, with primarily mechanical changes if they were needed. Level 2 is expanded to allow physical interaction with spirits in twilight. Level 3 allows an area to be made resonant, but it also only allows side stepping in certain locations. Level 4 is the only power that's radically different. The update has it transform your viate into a universal spirit bane and some ways you can use that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You use it to fight enemy spirits, yes, but also to make spirits your <i>allies</i> and bring them into Twilight where they can use their power in ways that serve you both. And one of the main things preventing a spirit from being able to follow an ally from the Shadow Realm into Twilight and aid them is a lack of Influence Conditions to sustain them where they go. If you've got a source of no-cost, universal Influence Conditions tagged onto a basic action you're already taking all the time, the role of using your Discipline as an art of mediumship is obviated. </div> </div> </div>You can already do that. If it's a spirit of fear you can simply scare the person, if it's a spirit of joy you can feed on the person, etc. It won't make them open, but it will make them resonant and the spirit can use it's influence to make them open. Remember, resonance is common, people are resonant with something almost all the time, and probably with quite a few things. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it makes for a lot more interesting play if your vampire is courting spirit allies and ushering them through Twilight to use their power on her behalf </div> </div> </div>And making people resonant and open plays into that. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> rather than having extra bolt-on powers that just let her internalize the spirits' powers directly. </div> </div> </div>Are you still talking about Level 1 or have you shifted your complaints to levels 4 and 5 now? Level 4 is probably the power I'm least enthused with, I really didn't know what I wanted to do with it. For level 5 I ripped off the Dragolescu bloodline's 5th point of Essentiaphagia from Bloodlines the Devoted. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's also a bit much to stack on top of the bloodline bane I suggested, which already has <i>you</i> acting as a magnet for a bunch of spirits with vampire-adjacent resonance. Too much resonance all the time. </div> </div> </div>That's a fair argument. On the other hand it can also allow the spirits you're attracting additional options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}